cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Lifeline, please cite it as below."
title: "Lifeline: resupply planning by truck, drone and airdrop on real terrain, roads, weather and satellite imagery"
type: software
authors:
  - alias: sekaikx
repository-code: "https://github.com/sekaikx/Trajectory-and-Airdrop-Simulator"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-15
abstract: >-
  Lifeline is a desktop planner for humanitarian and contested resupply. For
  each delivery it compares a truck on the OpenStreetMap road network, a
  drone, and a parachute airdrop with a computed release point, using real
  elevation, wind forecasts and line-of-sight exposure, and schedules the
  fleet by priority, deadline, risk tolerance and cost. A flood check marks
  newly flooded land in Sentinel-2 imagery with a water index or a U-Net
  trained on Sen1Floods11.
keywords:
  - humanitarian logistics
  - disaster response
  - airdrop
  - drone delivery
  - route planning
  - flood mapping
  - Sentinel-2
  - OpenStreetMap
